{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile + scvi_n200 is the clear winner so far (config_005/006 at ~0.65), and the multiprofile effect is large (~0.13 gain over singleprofile). Aggregation (avgpool vs transformer) makes negligible difference. The image modality appears weak (resnet50 image-only at 0.208). Uncertainty: We have not tested whether scgpt, a more specialized RNA foundation-model encoder, can outperform scvi_n200 in the multiprofile setting. Question: config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) directly compares against config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) by changing only the RNA encoder, cleanly isolating the encoder effect. Why best next: This is a single-variable, high-information experiment in the most promising region. If scgpt improves, we gain a new best and a direction to extend into multimodal; if it matches or lags, we confirm scvi_n200 is near-optimal and can redirect budget toward testing whether a better image encoder (ViT-L) or multimodal fusion adds value on top of the RNA signal. It avoids the risk of spending a run on a multimodal config that adds complexity while the RNA encoder question remains open."
}

